== 3.9 Chapter 3 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Insurance is best described as],
  [a form of saving],
  [a government tax],
  [a gamble],
  [the pooling of similar risks so that many small premiums meet one large loss]
)

#mcq(2, [The principle that requires the insured to have something to lose is],
  [contribution],
  [insurable interest],
  [indemnity],
  [subrogation]
)

#mcq(3, [The principle that limits a claim to the value of the loss is],
  [indemnity],
  [proximate cause],
  [contribution],
  [utmost good faith]
)

#mcq(4, [The principle that requires full disclosure of material facts is],
  [indemnity],
  [contribution],
  [subrogation],
  [utmost good faith]
)

#mcq(5, [After paying a claim, an insurer may sue the party at fault. This is],
  [reinsurance],
  [contribution],
  [subrogation],
  [indemnity]
)

#mcq(6, [Where two policies cover the same risk, the insurers share the loss. This is],
  [reinsurance],
  [subrogation],
  [contribution],
  [double indemnity]
)

#mcq(7, [The principle that the nearest cause of the loss must be a covered peril is],
  [proximate cause],
  [indemnity],
  [utmost good faith],
  [insurable interest]
)

#mcq(8, [A trader's stock is worth ₦10 million and is insured for ₦6 million. A fire destroys stock worth ₦2 million. He recovers],
  [₦1.0 million],
  [₦2.0 million],
  [₦0.6 million],
  [₦1.2 million]
)

#mcq(9, [Stock worth ₦8 million insured for ₦6 million suffers a ₦4 million loss. The payment is],
  [₦3 million],
  [₦6 million],
  [₦2 million],
  [₦4 million]
)

#mcq(10, [Stock worth ₦5 million insured for ₦4 million suffers a ₦2.5 million loss. The payment is],
  [₦1.5 million],
  [₦3.0 million],
  [₦2.0 million],
  [₦2.5 million]
)

#mcq(11, [The clause that reduces a claim because the sum insured is below the value at risk is the],
  [renewal clause],
  [excess clause],
  [arbitration clause],
  [average clause]
)

#mcq(12, [A policy that pays only if the insured dies within a stated period is],
  [term assurance],
  [whole-life assurance],
  [endowment],
  [annuity]
)

#mcq(13, [A policy that pays at death or at the end of the term, whichever comes first, is],
  [marine insurance],
  [term assurance],
  [endowment],
  [whole-life assurance]
)

#mcq(14, [An annuity is],
  [a reinsurance treaty],
  [a loan against a policy],
  [a lump sum paid to an insurer in return for an income],
  [a policy that pays a lump sum on death]
)

#mcq(15, [Life assurance is not a contract of indemnity because],
  [life is short],
  [premiums are high],
  [the insurer may refuse],
  [a life cannot be valued in money]
)

#mcq(16, [Reinsurance is],
  [insurance taken out by an insurer],
  [a government scheme],
  [a second policy for the insured],
  [double insurance]
)

#mcq(17, [A person who insures the same property with two companies may],
  [collect nothing],
  [collect once, the insurers contributing],
  [collect twice],
  [choose either policy and ignore the other]
)

#mcq(18, [A warehouse holding imported goods on which duty has not been paid is insured under],
  [fire and property insurance],
  [employers' liability],
  [fidelity guarantee],
  [marine insurance]
)

#mcq(19, [Insurance against loss caused by a dishonest employee is],
  [marine insurance],
  [fidelity guarantee],
  [employers' liability],
  [public liability]
)

#mcq(20, [Employers' liability insurance covers],
  [damage to the employer's own goods],
  [claims by employees injured at work],
  [bad debts],
  [loss of profit]
)

#mcq(21, [The proposal form is important because],
  [it records the facts on which the insurer assesses the risk],
  [it cancels the policy],
  [it pays the claim],
  [it is the policy]
)

#mcq(22, [A cover note gives],
  [a discount],
  [a refund],
  [permanent cover],
  [temporary cover while the proposal is considered]
)

#mcq(23, [An excess on a policy is],
  [a bonus],
  [a tax],
  [the first part of each loss that the insured bears],
  [the premium]
)

#mcq(24, [A peril excluded from a fire policy is],
  [arson by the insured],
  [a short circuit],
  [explosion of a domestic cooker],
  [lightning]
)

#mcq(25, [The risk that cannot be insured is one that is],
  [certain to happen],
  [shared by many similar risks],
  [uncertain and independent],
  [measurable]
)

#mcq(26, [Insurance works best when the risks insured are],
  [very few],
  [many, similar and independent],
  [certain],
  [all alike in one place]
)

#mcq(27, [The party who assesses a loss on behalf of the insurer is the],
  [loss adjuster],
  [broker],
  [agent],
  [underwriter]
)

#mcq(28, [An insurance broker differs from an agent because the broker],
  [works for one insurer],
  [acts for the insured],
  [pays the claims],
  [sets the premium]
)

#mcq(29, [A marine policy covering cargo from Lagos to Rotterdam is],
  [a valued policy],
  [a floating policy],
  [a time policy],
  [a voyage policy]
)

#mcq(30, [A policy that states the agreed value of the subject matter in advance is],
  [a valued policy],
  [an unvalued policy],
  [a blanket policy],
  [a floating policy]
)

#mcq(31, [Whose responsibility is it to disclose material facts?],
  [the insured],
  [the broker only],
  [the insurer only],
  [the loss adjuster]
)

#mcq(32, [A trader insures his shop for ₦3 million and it is destroyed by fire. The shop was worth ₦3 million but earned ₦500,000 profit a year. He recovers],
  [₦2.5 million],
  [₦3 million],
  [₦500,000],
  [₦3.5 million]
)

#mcq(33, [Insurance premiums are paid in advance because],
  [the law requires it],
  [insurers need the interest],
  [the broker is paid first],
  [the pool must exist before the loss]
)

#mcq(34, [Which risk would an insurer refuse?],
  [fire in a warehouse],
  [the theft of a car],
  [the outbreak of war in the country],
  [injury to a worker]
)

#mcq(35, [A no-claim discount is],
  [a penalty],
  [a commission],
  [an excess],
  [a reduction in premium for a claim-free period]
)

#mcq(36, [Which class of insurance is transacted by a life office rather than a general insurer?],
  [marine],
  [fire],
  [life assurance],
  [motor]
)

#mcq(37, [The sum insured is],
  [the premium],
  [the excess],
  [the commission],
  [the maximum the insurer will pay under the policy]
)

#mcq(38, [If a policy is avoided for non-disclosure, the insurer],
  [must renew it],
  [pays half the claim],
  [may treat the contract as never having existed],
  [pays the premium only]
)

#mcq(39, [The person who calculates the premium and decides whether to accept a risk is the],
  [broker],
  [actuary only],
  [adjuster],
  [underwriter]
)

#mcq(40, [Insurance creates security for trade because it],
  [increases profit directly],
  [raises prices],
  [reduces tax],
  [removes the fear of a ruinous loss from the trader]
)

